# pitest02-card.list -- what tools/sync-card.sh puts onto the owner's Pi card for the collected real-Pi run (PITEST02).
# Format: tools/sync-card.sh header. The kernel is not in this list: `--kernels <run>/kernels --active kern1119.img` adds it
# (BOOT:kern1119.img + BOOT:kernel8.img; the old kernel8.img, cmdline.txt, config.txt are saved to card-before/ first).
# cmdline.txt is NOT touched by the write. CMD32.TXT / CMD16.TXT are plain files beside it: the owner copies one over
# CMDLINE.TXT to switch the boot configuration (TESTBLATT.md, "Umschalten").
# Every source below lies in this run directory (payload/); the built programs are from the worktree of afc2bb1c0
# (method/build-notes.txt). Files the card already has stay untouched unless they are named here.
BOOT:CMD32.TXT                    | measurements/measurement-2026-11-19-pitest02-prep/payload/boot/CMD32.TXT          | method file (vdiplanes=32)
BOOT:CMD16.TXT                    | measurements/measurement-2026-11-19-pitest02-prep/payload/boot/CMD16.TXT          | method file (vdiplanes=16)
BOOT:CMDSER.TXT                   | measurements/measurement-2026-11-19-pitest02-prep/payload/boot/CMDSER.TXT         | method file (serial=on, only with a USB-TTL adapter)
BOOT:CMD32S.TXT                   | measurements/measurement-2026-11-19-pitest02-prep/payload/boot/CMD32S.TXT         | method file (serial=on vdiplanes=32, only with a USB-TTL adapter)
# --- probes (C:\PITEST) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C:\PITEST\SNDTONE.NCP             | measurements/measurement-2026-11-19-pitest02-prep/payload/pitest/SNDTONE.NCP      | sdk/build.sh sdk/examples/sndtone.c SNDTONE.NCP
